<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhanguo ce</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a> · Also known as Strategies of the Warring States, Zhan Guo Ce</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Zhanguo ce, or Strategies of the Warring States, is a Chinese collection of speeches, anecdotes and diplomatic schemes from the fifth to the third century BCE, arranged by state. It was compiled by the Han scholar Liu Xiang in the first century BCE from earlier materials. Although often rhetorical rather than strictly factual, it is a major source for the politics of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warring-states-period">Warring States period</a>.</p></div>
